    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333619/comment/12379404",
          "id": "12379404",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=becke%40u.washington.edu",
            "name": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "key": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael Becke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "I'd like to go ahead and tackle this one, but I need a little clarification. \nDoes the following correctly describe what we want?\n\n- we want to perform a get on www.google.com, let's say www.google.com has X > 1\nIP addresses \n- we want to specify which IP address x to actually connect to\n- we want www.google.com in the Http header instead of x\n\nIf this is the case, it sounds like we may want support for custom DNS\nresolution.  Though this might be a little more than is needed for this simple\ncase I think that is what it boils down to.\n\nMike\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=becke%40u.washington.edu",
            "name": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "key": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael Becke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2003-02-28T02:37:16.000+0000",
          "updated": "2003-02-28T02:37:16.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333619/comment/12379405",
          "id": "12379405",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jsdever%40apache.org",
            "name": "jsdever@apache.org",
            "key": "jsdever@apache.org",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Jeff Dever",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "I think the idea is more one ip -> multiple hosts.\n\nGET HTTP/1.1 216.239.39.101/\nHost: www.google.com\n\n\nGET HTTP/1.1 216.239.39.101/\nHost: www.google.ca\n\nMight be a non-issue.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jsdever%40apache.org",
            "name": "jsdever@apache.org",
            "key": "jsdever@apache.org",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Jeff Dever",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2003-02-28T06:14:41.000+0000",
          "updated": "2003-02-28T06:14:41.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333619/comment/12379406",
          "id": "12379406",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ortwin Glueck",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "An easy solution would be to create means to set IP and Host header field\nseparately (so no implicit DNS lookup ever occurs).\n\nThis approach would separate HttpClient from the DNS lookup if needed. If\nsomeone wants to use a custom DNS lookup method he can do it, but HttpClient\ndoesn't have to care about.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ortwin Glueck",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "created": "2003-02-28T16:51:20.000+0000",
          "updated": "2003-02-28T16:51:20.000+0000"
        },
